Package: violoop-edge-kiosk-qt
Version: 0.0.0
Section: graphics
Priority: optional
Architecture: ARCH_PLACEHOLDER
Maintainer: doctor <doctor@bvio.ai>
Depends: violoop-qt6 (>= 6.8.5-violoop3), weston, fonts-noto-cjk, fonts-noto-core, fonts-dejavu-core, fonts-noto-color-emoji, libstdc++6
Description: Violoop Edge device kiosk UI (Qt/QML, evaluation build)
 Qt/QML reimplementation of the device kiosk front-end, evaluating
 replacing the production Flutter app (violoop-edge-front /
 violoop-edge-kiosk.service, see sibling violoop-edge-front2). Installs
 alongside it, not in place of it - no Provides/Replaces/Conflicts
 against that package. This package's own violoop-edge-kiosk-qt.service
 is NOT enabled automatically on install (see postinst): both kiosk
 apps bind the same seat0/tty7 and cannot run at once, so an operator
 must explicitly choose which one is active.
 .
 Links against /opt/violoop-qt6 (package violoop-qt6), BvioTech's own
 Qt 6.8.5 build with the GLES/ESSL100 and qtquicktimeline fixes this
 repo's qt3d-spike found necessary on this device - not the Debian
 system qt6-* packages, which reproduce that bug.
